# The knowledge graph itself IS committed (graph.json, graph.html, GRAPH_REPORT.md,
# manifest.json, cost.json) — see ../CLAUDE.md. Only machine-specific or regenerated
# sidecars are ignored so the committed graph stays portable.
#
# NOTE: cache/ is ignored below per PR #1 review feedback, which contradicts ../CLAUDE.md's
# current text (still says cache/ is committed). Flagged as a follow-up to reconcile the
# doc, not resolved here.

# Absolute, per-machine pointers written on each run
.graphify_python
.graphify_root

# Internal labeling sidecar — regenerated every build
.graphify_labels.json

# Transient per-build temp files (normally auto-cleaned)
.graphify_detect.*
.graphify_*.tmp
.needs_update

# Regenerated AST/analysis cache — not part of the portable graph output
cache/

# Dated run archives graphify writes beside the current outputs — local history of
# past builds, not the graph itself. The committed graph is the top-level one.
20[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]/
